  "theorem_statement": "The nonidentity stabilizer of the complete registered multiplier assignment is the exact fiber-product element with S5 coordinate (0 1)(2 3), fixing 4, and D8 coordinate rotation 2 with no flip. Its induced K6 action is (0 1)(2 3), fixing points 4 and 5. It exchanges the two endpoints 2 and 3 of the multiplier root duad, exchanges exceptional point 0 with point 1, and fixes the reconstructed C33 point 4. It centralizes the native V4 deck group pointwise and is therefore not the native b/ab character-exchange involution. Relative to the exported representative chart, it acts by its base involution together with an exact nonconstant local V4 translation. On the twenty-four registered lifted ten-cycles it fixes eight and exchanges eight pairs.",
  "verdict": "assignment_mirror_is_diagonal_s5_double_transposition_d8_half_turn_lift"
